SUMMARY:Fairhope Farmers Market: Fall Season
DESCRIPTION:The Fairhope Farmers Market sets up behind the Fairhope Public
  Library at Bancroft Street and Magnolia Avenue every Thursday afternoon 
 this fall\, from 2 PM to 6 PM. Tables carry local produce\, baked goods\,
  plants\, honey and handmade goods from a rotating group of vendors. The 
 season runs through November 12\, when the market closes an hour earlier 
 at 5 PM\, and eligible seniors can use the Alabama Senior Farmers Market 
 Nutrition Program card at participating stalls.\nPrice: not published by 
 the venue\, so confirm before you go\nArea: Mobile & Baldwin County\nTime
 s: Thursday 9/10 · 2:00 PM to 6:00 PM\nhttps://coastaleventures.com/even
 ts/ev-fairhope-farmers-market-fall-season-0910.html
